# {{product}}: k6 load tests

- `lib/` is rendered by the framework's `scripts/foundation.mjs` from its `templates/k6/` (files marked "Generated by
  scripts/foundation.mjs"; don't edit them). `lib/ext/` holds hand-written additions; `scripts/` holds one script
  per workload scenario.
- Product choices (the auth scheme, base path, default headers) live in `artifacts/{{product}}/foundation/k6-overlay.json`.

## Environment

| Variable | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `BASE_URL` | the target; there is no default |
| `K6_ALLOWED_HOSTS` | comma-separated hosts load may be sent to; `setup()` aborts unless BASE_URL's host is listed |
| `ATF_MODE` | `full-run` lets mutating scenarios run; anything else aborts them |
| `K6_USER`, `K6_PASSWORD`, `K6_TOKEN` | credentials for the auth scheme in `lib/settings.js`; never literals |
| `K6_SCRIPT` | the script's name, for `results/<script>.summary.json` and `.created.json` |

## Running

```
ATF_MODE=full-run BASE_URL=<target> K6_ALLOWED_HOSTS=<target host> K6_SCRIPT=<m>-<scenario> k6 run scripts/<m>-<scenario>.js
k6 inspect scripts/<m>-<scenario>.js
```

## Safety

- Every script's `setup()` calls `assertAllowedHost()` and `requireFullRun(<mutates>)` from `lib/config.js`.
- Live load runs only in full-run runs; readonly runs only `k6 inspect` the scripts.
- A mutating scenario deletes what it creates in the same iteration. Anything it could not delete goes through
  `trackLeftover(type, ref)` from `lib/data.js`; `handleSummary` writes those to `results/<script>.created.json`,
  and the runner records them in the framework's ledger.
